      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "Lars von Trier's The Kingdom (1994) revolutionized supernatural hospital drama by blending Gothic horror with pitch-black comedy. Shot with handheld cameras and a sickly sepia tone, this Danish miniseries turns Copenhagen's largest hospital into a nightmarish labyrinth where the boundaries between life and death blur. Like <a href=\"/movie/1062861\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"1062861\">Twin Peaks</a> (1990), it uses supernatural elements to expose institutional corruption, while its medical setting recalls <a href=\"/movie/651\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"651\">MASH</a> (1970) in its ability to find dark humor in professional environments."
      },
      {
        "type": "movies",
        "movies": [
          {
