          },
          {
            "title": "Riget Exodus",
            "year": 2022,
            "slug": "Von Trier returns to the haunted hospital for a modern continuation of the original series",
            "poster": "/images/placeholder-poster.jpg",
            "initialStreaming": "MUBI",
            "tmdb_id": null
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "The series sparked a wave of medical horror that influenced works like <a href=\"/movie/375569\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"375569\">Kingdom Hospital</a> (2004), Stephen King's American adaptation, and the atmospheric dread of <a href=\"/movie/10972\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"10972\">Session 9</a> (2001). Von Trier's signature shaky-cam aesthetic and mixing of genres would later define the Dogme 95 movement, seen in films like <a href=\"/movie/452\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"452\">The Idiots</a> (1998) and <a href=\"/movie/145\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"145\">Breaking the Waves</a> (1996). The series' ability to balance institutional critique with supernatural horror paved the way for works like <a href=\"/movie/9539\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"9539\">Martyrs</a> (2008) and <a href=\"/movie/575776\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"575776\">Saint Maud</a> (2020)."
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "What sets The Kingdom apart is its masterful blend of tones - shifting from bureaucratic satire to genuine horror seamlessly. The series influenced later works like <a href=\"/movie/15543\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"15543\">Penny Dreadful</a> (2014-2016) in its ability to create a Gothic atmosphere in a modern setting, while its commentary on medical institutions can be seen reflected in films like The Autopsy of Jane Doe (2016). SUBHEAD: Impact on Medical Horror Genre"
      },
      {
